{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>You shall not add.</b> Upon which, if you add you subtract, for all who add detract — for if you make five tzitzit you have also detracted from the four, since they are nothing given that you did not fulfill the commandment properly. And likewise Rashi explained: five passages in tefillin and five species in the lulav. But if one sat in the sukkah for eight days, the eighth does not come with the seven, and what he did is done."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:25.961164537Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}